{"name":"Dark Tone Ink","hex":"#121212","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dark","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having an absolute or (more often) relative lack of light.","Extinguished."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A complete or (more often) partial absence of light.","Ignorance."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dark"},{"term":"tone","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A specific pitch.","(in the diatonic scale) An interval of a major second."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["to give a particular tone to","to change the colour of"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tone"},{"term":"ink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A pigment (or dye)-based fluid used for writing, printing etc.","A particular type, color or container of this fluid."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To apply ink to; to cover or smear with ink.","To sign (a contract or similar document)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ink","blocks":[{"text":"Ink is a gel, sol, or solution that contains at least one colorant, such as a dye or pigment, and is used to color a surface to produce an image, text, or design. Ink is used for drawing or writing with a pen, brush, reed pen, or quill. Thicker inks, in paste form, are used extensively in letterpress and lithographic printing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/F%C3%BCller-tinte_hg.jpg/330px-F%C3%BCller-tinte_hg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ink"},{"title":"Darkness","blocks":[{"text":"Darkness is the condition resulting from a lack of illumination, or an absence of visible light."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Creation_of_Light.png/330px-Creation_of_Light.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darkness"},{"title":"Tint, shade and tone","blocks":[{"text":"In color theory, a tint is a mixture of a color with white, which increases lightness, while a shade is a mixture with black, which increases darkness. A tone is produced either by mixing a color with gray, or by both tinting and shading. Mixing a color with any neutral color reduces the chroma, or colorfulness, while the perceived hue can be affected slightly."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Tint-tone-shade.svg/330px-Tint-tone-shade.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tint%2C_shade_and_tone"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/%D7%A7%D7%9C%D7%A3%2C_%D7%A0%D7%95%D7%A6%D7%94_%D7%95%D7%93%D7%99%D7%95.jpg/500px-%D7%A7%D7%9C%D7%A3%2C_%D7%A0%D7%95%D7%A6%D7%94_%D7%95%D7%93%D7%99%D7%95.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/%D7%A7%D7%9C%D7%A3%2C_%D7%A0%D7%95%D7%A6%D7%94_%D7%95%D7%93%D7%99%D7%95.jpg/1280px-%D7%A7%D7%9C%D7%A3%2C_%D7%A0%D7%95%D7%A6%D7%94_%D7%95%D7%93%D7%99%D7%95.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/%D7%A7%D7%9C%D7%A3%2C_%D7%A0%D7%95%D7%A6%D7%94_%D7%95%D7%93%D7%99%D7%95.jpg/500px-%D7%A7%D7%9C%D7%A3%2C_%D7%A0%D7%95%D7%A6%D7%94_%D7%95%D7%93%D7%99%D7%95.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Writing ink and a quill","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A%D7%A7%D7%9C%D7%A3%2C_%D7%A0%D7%95%D7%A6%D7%94_%D7%95%D7%93%D7%99%D7%95.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Ganesha_ink.jpg/330px-Ganesha_ink.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Ganesha_ink.jpg/330px-Ganesha_ink.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ink drawing of Ganesha under an umbrella (early 19th century). Ink, called masi, an admixture of several chemical components, has been used in India since at least the 4th century BC.[2] The practice of writing with ink and a sharp pointed needle was common in early South India.[3] Several Jain sutras in India were compiled in ink.[4]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGanesha_ink.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/BlackInkBottle.JPG/500px-BlackInkBottle.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/BlackInkBottle.JPG/1280px-BlackInkBottle.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/BlackInkBottle.JPG/500px-BlackInkBottle.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Black ink bottle","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlackInkBottle.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Oak_galls_and_iron%28II%29_sulfate_-_California_State_Archives.jpg/500px-Oak_galls_and_iron%28II%29_sulfate_-_California_State_Archives.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Oak_galls_and_iron%28II%29_sulfate_-_California_State_Archives.jpg/1280px-Oak_galls_and_iron%28II%29_sulfate_-_California_State_Archives.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Oak_galls_and_iron%28II%29_sulfate_-_California_State_Archives.jpg/500px-Oak_galls_and_iron%28II%29_sulfate_-_California_State_Archives.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Oak galls and iron(II) sulfate","link":"https